The thick section of the graph below is the piece of $y=\cos x$ that has been kept.
Which interval is it?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-7.4, xmax=7.4, ymin=-2.6, ymax=1.7, samples=150, clip=false, width=12cm, height=7cm, xtick={-6.2832,-3.1416,3.1416,6.2832}, xticklabels={$-2\pi$,$-\pi$,$\pi$,$2\pi$}, ytick={-1,1}, every tick label/.style={font=\scriptsize}]
\addplot[thick, <->, domain=-7.4:7.4] {cos(deg(x))};
\addplot[very thick, red, domain=3.1416:6.2832] {cos(deg(x))};
\node[red, font=\small] at (axis cs:0,-2.2) {thick section};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
